/-!
# The ATLAS degree-276 permutation model of the third Conway group

`TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3` is the subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 276)` generated by the
literal forward images in the ATLAS files `Co3G1-p276B0.m1` and `Co3G1-p276B0.m2`.
The file points `1, …, 276` become `0, …, 275`. Both inverse tables are included,
so that products and inverses of the generators compute directly. Multiplication
follows Mathlib's convention, `(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`.

The generators have orders `3` and `4`, and their product has order `14`.
The model acts transitively, so the first basic orbit in an order computation has
length `276`. No order of the group or relationship with a presented group is
asserted here.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3`: the subgroup generated by the two file permutations.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.orderOf_a`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.orderOf_b`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.orderOf_a_mul_b`: the generator-order checks.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co3.instIsPretransitive`: transitivity of the model.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `Co3G1-p276B0`. Forward image files:
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/Co3/mtx/Co3G1-p276B0.m1> and
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/Co3/mtx/Co3G1-p276B0.m2>.
-/

public section

